  "outcome": "Use Seneca.js with entity-based data model (pqs/asset, sys/user, etc.) for backend communication. Message patterns for non-CRUD operations.",
  "rationale": "Flexible message pattern routing, entity-based CRUD is intuitive, backend can change without frontend changes, custom middleware for cross-cutting concerns, browser compatible.",
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "acceptance": "Seneca.js less common than REST/GraphQL (team unfamiliarity, limited ecosystem). Migration to REST would require significant refactoring (100+ calls). Acceptable tradeoff for flexibility and microservice architecture."
  },
